From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: marty <marty@fyai.co.nz>
Date: Sun, 7 Sep 2026 12:40:00 +1200
Subject: [PATCH] Games: dispatch the hardware context reset from GetBuffer()

Patch 1030 moved the reset out of OpenStream() and into RunFrame(). That fixed
the framebuffer being reported as 0, and replaced a black screen with a
segfault.

Mupen64Plus-Next connects its video plugin from inside context_reset:
context_reset() -> reinit_gfx_plugin() -> emu_step_initialize() ->
plugin_connect_all(), which is what assigns `gfx = gfx_gln64`. Its retro_run()
then runs the emulator with no guard, so main_run() reaches `if (!gfx.romOpen())`
with the whole function table still zeroed and calls through a null pointer:

    #0  0x0000000000000000
    #1  game.libretro.mupen64plus-nx.so
    #3  retro_run ()

The reset has to happen before the client's first frame, and RunFrame() is too
late by one frame: the client opens its stream from *inside* that first
retro_run - glsm_ctl(GLSM_CTL_STATE_BIND) precedes co_switch() to the emulator
thread - so the flag RunFrame() reads is not set until after the frame it would
have dispatched in. The log shows the two, half a millisecond apart and on one
thread:

    RetroPlayer[RENDERING]: Render manager configured
    mupen64plus: [EmuThread] M64CMD_EXECUTE

Dispatching it where 1030 originally did does not work either, and that is the
whole reason 1030 exists: OpenStream() runs inside the add-on's CStream::Open(),
which assigns m_handle from that call's *return value*, so every callback the
add-on makes during it is refused by its own `if (!m_handle) return false`.

GetBuffer() is the one point where both hold. It is reached from
GLSM_CTL_STATE_BIND, so CStream::Open() has returned and the handle is live,
and it is still ahead of co_switch() and therefore ahead of romOpen(). The
dispatch clears its own flag before calling out, so the get_current_framebuffer()
the reset itself provokes re-enters here harmlessly.

RunFrame() keeps its call as a fallback for a client that never asks for a
buffer.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 xbmc/games/addons/streams/GameClientStreamHwFramebuffer.cpp | 8 ++++++++
 xbmc/games/addons/streams/GameClientStreamHwFramebuffer.h   | 9 +++++++++
 2 files changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/xbmc/games/addons/streams/GameClientStreamHwFramebuffer.cpp b/xbmc/games/addons/streams/GameClientStreamHwFramebuffer.cpp
--- a/xbmc/games/addons/streams/GameClientStreamHwFramebuffer.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/games/addons/streams/GameClientStreamHwFramebuffer.cpp
@@ -69,6 +69,24 @@
                                   static_cast<RETRO::StreamBuffer&>(hwFramebufferBuffer)))
     {
       buffer.hw_framebuffer.framebuffer = hwFramebufferBuffer.framebuffer;
+
+      // Deliver the context reset here, and not before the lookup above.
+      //
+      // It cannot be delivered where it is requested, in OpenStream(): that
+      // runs inside the add-on's CStream::Open(), which assigns its handle from
+      // that call's return value, so the add-on refuses every callback made
+      // during it. Kodi holds the request until a buffer is asked for, which is
+      // the first point the handle is live.
+      //
+      // After the lookup rather than before it, because the lookup is what
+      // makes the pool's GL context current on this thread. A client sets its
+      // renderer up inside context_reset, so a reset delivered ahead of that
+      // runs every one of its GL calls against no current context.
+      //
+      // The flag is cleared before the reset is delivered, so the
+      // get_current_framebuffer() the reset provokes re-enters here harmlessly.
+      m_callback.DispatchPendingHardwareContextReset();
+
       return true;
     }
   }
diff --git a/xbmc/games/addons/streams/GameClientStreamHwFramebuffer.h b/xbmc/games/addons/streams/GameClientStreamHwFramebuffer.h
--- a/xbmc/games/addons/streams/GameClientStreamHwFramebuffer.h
+++ b/xbmc/games/addons/streams/GameClientStreamHwFramebuffer.h
@@ -35,6 +35,15 @@
    * Any GL state is lost, and must not be deinitialized explicitly.
    */
   virtual void HardwareContextReset() = 0;
+
+  /*!
+   * \brief Deliver a context reset that was requested while the add-on was
+   *        still opening its stream
+   *
+   * Does nothing if none is pending. Safe to call re-entrantly: the pending
+   * flag is cleared before the reset is delivered.
+   */
+  virtual void DispatchPendingHardwareContextReset() = 0;
 };
 
 class CGameClientStreamHwFramebuffer : public IGameClientStream
